id: power-shot
name: Power Shot
kind: signature
side: advantages
tpCost: 4
tpCostPerRank: 4, 6, 8
ranks: 3
requirement: This Signature Technique does not have the Low Penetration Disadvantage.
description: >
  Your Signature Technique hits harder, by a rank at a time: 2(T) on its Wound Roll
  for each rank bought. The ranks are what a Parry or a Deflect has to answer.
text: >
  Power Shot: Your signature technique has more power.
  –TP Cost: 4 (First Rank), 6 (Second Rank), 8 (Third Rank)
  –Requirement: This Signature Technique does not have the Low Penetration
  Disadvantage.
  –Effect: Increase your Wound Rolls for this Signature Technique by 2(T) for each
  rank of this Advantage.

---

# No script. What this does is add to the Wound Roll of the attack that carries it,
# and an Advantage is not something a character holds - it is something an attack was
# built with, so it is read where the attack is rolled rather than off a sheet.
#
# --- The first feature with ranks -------------------------------------------------
#
# Every other one is had or not had. This one is had one, two or three times, and
# what it is worth is counted per rank - so a Maneuver carries it once per rank, and
# the rank is how many times it is in the list. `advantages.includes("power-shot")`
# goes on answering "does this attack have it" for anything that only wants to know
# that, and `featureRanks` is what asks how many.
#
# `ranks: 3` is the ceiling the entry names by listing three prices and no fourth.
#
# --- What the ranks cost ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# "4 (First Rank), 6 (Second Rank), 8 (Third Rank)", kept here as written. Whether
# the third rank costs 8 or costs 4+6+8 is not something the entry settles, and
# nothing in this system spends Technique Points yet - so the three numbers are
# carried as they are printed and the sum is the table's until there is something
# here to spend against.
#
# --- The Requirement, which cannot be checked -------------------------------------
#
# "This Signature Technique does not have the Low Penetration Disadvantage." There is
# no Low Penetration Disadvantage in this system - the Disadvantages folder holds one
# file, All or Nothing - so there is nothing to check this against. The requirement
# is carried as written and shown wherever a feature's requirement is shown, which is
# what can honestly be done until that file exists.
#
# --- Where the ranks are answered --------------------------------------------------
#
# The Wound Roll is one place. The other two are somebody else's rolls: the Parry
# option of the Defend Maneuver reduces its Dice Score "by 1(bT) for each Energy
# Charge or rank of Power Shot on the Attacking Maneuver", and the Deflect and
# Distant Deflect options of the Intervene Maneuver do the same in (T). Both of those
# have been written for a rank count since they were built and had none to read.
